Package: multiGGM
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Inference of Multiple Gaussian Graphical Models
Version: 0.10.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Margaret", family = "Janiczek", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "mjaniczek@umass.edu"),
    person(given = "Claudio", family = "Busatto", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Author of the mGHS sampler adapted in src/; see inst/mghs/UPSTREAM.md"))
Description: Bayesian inference of multiple Gaussian graphical models, one
    network per group, with Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) samplers that
    borrow strength across groups. Supports the G-Wishart prior with a Markov
    random field (MRF) prior on the graphs (Peterson, Stingo and Vannucci
    (2015) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2014.896806>), a scalable spike-and-slab
    prior (Shaddox et al. (2018) <doi:10.1007/s12561-016-9176-6>), its
    extension to multiple data platforms (Shaddox et al. (2020)
    <doi:10.1093/biostatistics/kxy078>), and the multiple graphical horseshoe
    (Busatto and Stingo (2025) <doi:10.1080/10618600.2024.2435480>). Edge and
    differential-edge probabilities are kept as running sums during sampling,
    so large networks can be analysed without storing draws. Includes Bayesian
    false discovery rate selection, a permutation null for choosing the
    minimum difference of interest, convergence diagnostics, posterior
    predictive checks and parallel multi-chain runs.
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0.0)
